   568	    rewrites its cache every step — the most expensive case — showed ~540 prompt tokens
   569	    per step and looked the cheapest. Those twelve episodes were discarded and re-run.
   570	    The §4 table does not depend on it: it was computed by the grid runner, which counted
   571	    writes.
   572	
   573	11. **A probe that could not fail.** The first L2 scorer counted dependent steps on a
   574	    simulated trajectory and subtracted only deaf actions, and its runner repaired the
   575	    world whenever the runtime returned no action; a runtime that never answers scored
   576	    100 %. It was the section of this draft we had checked least, because its result was
   577	    the cleanest. The fifth adversarial review found it. Re-measured with the decisive
   578	    step read from the real trajectory, explicit state goes from "132 of 132" to 70 of
   579	    72 episodes. L1 had the same world-repairing runner and a second defect of design,
   580	    found by the sixth review: its fact was not delayed in two of its three scenarios.
   581	    It was redesigned and re-measured (§5).
   582	
   583	Items 5 and 6 were found by an **independent adversarial review of this draft against
   584	the raw traces**, not by us. That review also corrected the failure classification
   585	above, the maintenance-event range in §2, the compression factor in §3 and the sample
   586	size in §3. We recommend the procedure, not the anecdote: have something recompute every
   587	published figure from the artefacts, without access to the prose that justifies it.
   588	
   589	Why traces matter, verbatim from one episode: at step 12 the model stores the SKU of a
   590	different pallet; at step 16 it asserts *"Shelf 0 (SKU-F, stored in step 12)"* when it
   591	had itself stored SKU-B there. **The early error contaminates later decisions** — and
   592	that, not sampling noise, is what produces the tail.
   593	
   594	**The transferable claim**: the paper treats the runtime as neutral infrastructure — a
   595	merge operator, a patch format, a schema, a prompt order. In this project, individual
   596	runtime decisions moved results by amounts comparable to or larger than the difference
   597	between the methods being compared: the schema field decides 0 % versus 67 % on the
   598	dependent step (§5), and a parser that silently dropped state patches decided what one
   599	of four arms measured until it was fixed (§6, item 7). We have not measured every such
   600	decision, so we make no claim about a general range.
   601	
   602	**Repository artefacts**: environment with fidelity flags, per-step traces, completeness
   603	verifier, a density meter that does not call the API, truncation counters, per-episode
   604	checkpointing and end-to-end cache accounting — except in the L1 aggregates, whose cost
   605	fields ignored cache reads and writes until the last re-measurement; its per-step traces
   606	record them and are the source to use.
   607	
   608	---
   609	
   610	## 7. Limitations
   611	
   612	- **`gemini-3-flash-preview` may not be their `Gemini-3-Flash`.** Declared as a risk
   613	  from the outset. Vertex returns the responding model ID on every call and it is
   614	  recorded per step, but not in the traces measured before that change. The Anthropic
   615	  client did not copy it until the last Stateful re-measurement: from then on — its 30
   616	  episodes and the prompt-order experiment — every step records
   617	  `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`; the earlier Haiku traces record only the requested alias
   618	  in their header.
   619	- **A reimplemented environment is not their environment.** We matched what their
   620	  appendix allows us to compare, and the remaining differences are in §2. The shelf
   621	  choice in `Store` still awaits an answer from the authors.
   622	- **Our Memory is not comparable to theirs.** Our summariser compresses fourteen times
   623	  more (5,770-token mean prompt against their 84,364 at T=200).
   624	  What we measured is our summarisation policy, not "summarisation" as a category.
   625	- **We have not proven the environment gaps have no effect.** The measured difference is
   626	  +0.009, with an interval of roughly −0.040 to +0.057 (§2): no change was detected, and
   627	  effects of several points in either direction remain compatible. The same caveat
   628	  applies to the three lowest noise levels in §3.
   629	- **Cell sizes are not uniform.** Nineteen cells carry 15 runs; ReAct at T=200 carries
   630	  19, unbalanced across seeds (3/3/7/3/3). Five of its episodes exist only as
   631	  aggregates, without traces.
   632	- **Cost figures price input only**, and the caching results depend on the length of the
   633	  static prefix (§4).
   634	- **The probes share cap and design across models, not decoding.** Both were re-measured
   635	  on all three models with the corrected runner (§5); Gemini runs with temperature 0 and
   636	  reasoning budget 0, Claude without either setting.
   637	- **One environment.** The second (Software Repository) was retired because it could not
   638	  measure what it was built for, not because the arms scored alike — they did not
   639	  (Haiku: SKILL.state 0.974, ReAct 0.895; Sonnet: 0.876 and 1.000, 9 episodes each). Its
   640	  dependency always sat exactly two steps after the event that created it, so it had no
   641	  delayed relevance to measure (`docs/resultados-bloque1.md`, §4.ter). We do not
   642	  attribute the score differences above to rule or routine steps: a separate diagnostic
   643	  sample of three episodes per arm shows both kinds of failure, and the nine-episode
   644	  cohorts themselves were not adjudicated.
   645	- **SKILL.state's ceiling depends on the model.** At 1.000 with zero variance on Gemini
   646	  the task did not discriminate at the top; on Haiku it does (0.958 at T=200), and the
   647	  failure is in writing the state (§3). Two models are not enough to say which models
   648	  make that error.
   649	- **Stateful has been re-measured only at T=50 and T=200**, with parser version 2 on
   650	  Gemini (which applied 3,748 of 3,750 of its patches) and version 3 on Haiku. The
   651	  intermediate horizons of Gemini's Table 1 keep the defective measurement, marked as
   652	  such.
   653	- **Haiku and Gemini do not share decoding settings** (§3): the cross-model differences
   654	  are between two configured systems, not two models under identical conditions.
   655	- **Haiku's Memory column mixes the summarisation policy with summary truncation** (§3);
   656	  the control arm has n=9 and bounds the effect at T=50 only.

